speechtext:
The
aggregate values of these tax expenditures in 1980, as given in the most recent tax expenditure account are as follows:
1.	Manufacturing:
(a)	lower corporate tax rate on manufacturing and processing profits, $600 million;
(b)	investment tax credit in the manufacturing sector, $170 million;
(c)	two-year write-off, $500 million.
2.	Small business:
(a)	reduced small business income tax rate, $1,200 million;
(b)	sales tax exemption, $20 million.
3.	Research and Development:
(a)	immediate write-off on R and D expenditures, $63 million;
(b)	allowance on incremental R and D, $34 million;
(c)	investment tax credit on R and D, $45 million.
4.	Resource Sector:

1.	(a) 232 Head office staff;
128	District office staff.
(b) 214 Head office staff;
129	District office staff.
2.	At Head office:
(a)	136;
(b)	1;
(c)	69;
2 French or English.
There are twenty-four commissioners appointed to the Canadian Pension Commission by order in council. These positions do not have a language designation. Because the Canadian Pension Commission is not scheduled to relocate to Prince Edward Island until 1983, staff have not yet been required to officially indicate their willingness to relocate. See also reply to question No. 82, part 4, answered July 2, 1980.

1.	(a) 33;
(b) 31.
2.	(a) 9;
(b)	None;
(c)	14.
There are eight employees who are order in council appointees and their positions do not have a language designation. The War Veterans Allowance Board officially relocated to Charlottetown, Prince Edward Island, in June, 1980.

February 13, 1981
Excise Tax
